{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531257-something-i-noticed-about-w5","id":1531257,"title":"Something I noticed about w5...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-21T17:00:32-08:00","id":1531257,"title":"Something I noticed about w5...","content":"I just wanna say that I'm more open to accept w5 flaws these days, but i also I'd like to say that after running it and reading the book a few times,i few like it's the best edition of wta for horror games.<br /> The problem is, when i say &quot;Horror games&quot; what i mean is &quot;games set <i>entirely </i>within the Horror Genre,without even a small huint of other genres&quot; if you try to insert a genre in a w5 game,a genre that inst' Horror,it just won't work. W5 doesn't do fantasy,w5 doesn't adventure and w5 certainly doesn't do any other genres,it's a Horror game,through and through. And that definitely is a problem<br /> I like it fine though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T18:57:24-08:00","id":1531263,"title":"","content":"That is presumably the end result of being bent and hammered into trying to fit W:tA into Vampire's<i> Enigma of Amigara Fault</i>-style hole, which itself cut a lot away from V:tM for V5. It's just more noticeable in Werewolf because Werewolf tried to present something like the later Exalted's &quot;Welcome to Creation, here's your shovel&quot; setup, where you could make headway into solving problems and not just dig the hole deeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T19:17:55-08:00","id":1531265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531257-something-i-noticed-about-w5?p=1531263#post1531263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is presumably the end result of being bent and hammered into trying to fit W:tA into Vampire's<i> Enigma of Amigara Fault</i>-style hole, which itself cut a lot away from V:tM for V5. It's just more noticeable in Werewolf because Werewolf tried to present something like the later Exalted's &quot;Welcome to Creation, here's your shovel&quot; setup, where you could make headway into solving problems and not just dig the hole deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>That comic scared me a lot as a kid","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T20:18:26-08:00","id":1531269,"title":"","content":"I generally agree with you. If you want to run a Werewolf horror game, W5 is better than the other editions. Typically with White Wolf games, when I wanted to run a game with a very specific theme of horror, I tended to use Wraith for that. I found Wraith slotted into the horror aspect better than any other game, due to the theme, concepts and mechanics. Hunter and Vampire were there second and third for horror games. Traditionally Werewolf games, for me, were always less about horror and more about ultra-violence, exploration and NPC ties.<br /> <br /> Exploration involving the Umbra was something only shifters could easily do, and it's an aspect that set them apart from the other gamelines, so I always leaned into it in my werewolf games and would usually have at least one or two major Umbral quests in a werewolf campaign. As for NPC ties, the other thing that set Werewolf apart from other games was the concept of kinfolk. Werewolves had strong, built-in ties to local communities of non-supernatural beings (often their own immediate family members). This tended to help keep werewolves linked to the setting in a way that other supernatural beings generally weren't.<br /> <br /> I'm still trying to get a handle on W5 edition. It's still got the ultra-violence of earlier editions, but it replaced the other two big aspects of the gameline with horror. Thing is, if I wanted to run a World of Darkness game with the specific theme of horror, I feel like H5 or V5 still do that better than W5. So I keep casting around trying to figure out why I would want to run a W5 game over a H5 or V5 game, and I keep coming back to the thing that sets W5 apart being that you turn into a giant furry rampage monster - which is cool, but ultimately I feel the gameline cut out a lot of the unique material that set it apart from other White Wolf games and focused on horror, which is something that the other existing gamelines still do better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T11:32:37-08:00","id":1531300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531257-something-i-noticed-about-w5?p=1531269#post1531269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still trying to get a handle on W5 edition. It's still got the ultra-violence of earlier editions, but it replaced the other two big aspects of the gameline with horror. Thing is, if I wanted to run a World of Darkness game with the specific theme of horror, I feel like H5 or V5 still do that better than W5. So I keep casting around trying to figure out why I would want to run a W5 game over a H5 or V5 game, and I keep coming back to the thing that sets W5 apart being that you turn into a giant furry rampage monster - which is cool, but ultimately I feel the gameline cut out a lot of the unique material that set it apart from other White Wolf games and focused on horror, which is something that the other existing gamelines still do better.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is houseruling, but; Remove tribes and auspices, remove the Wyrm and the umbra. The PCs have been bitten intentionally and are now being transported to a compound of a werewolf cult as the newest members. They escape, but find returning to normal life impossible with their Rage.<br /> <br /> That is how you do W5 horror,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T08:40:25-08:00","id":1531360,"title":"","content":"It's true that W5 works better as a horror-game and that's why I think it's so detrimental to the game how much legacy-stuff is still present in the game. It all would work better if there had been a far more radical shift in the game's premise if the focus is supposed to be a horror-game where you play a werewolf.<br /> <br /> But as far as the official representation is concerned, it will be interesting to see how the upcoming Scent Of Decay supplement imagines a typical W5 chronicle to be like. Especially since the first H5 supplement Lines Drawn In Blood wasn't exactly faithful to the H5 corebook either. That supplement subverts the corebook both in terms of rules and story. So I'm really curious about what the Renegade-writers' take on the W5 corebook will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T17:59:00-08:00","id":1531394,"title":"","content":"I mean theres already a bunch of stuff in the Renegade free handouts and scenarios that contradicts or goes against presentations in the corebook so.......I'm willing to bet it will be similar if not moreso to how LDiB treated H5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}